What was deferred at the end of Slice 4 vs. what shipped here
==============================================================
Slice 4 closed at 8/8 features but with three known gaps:

  1. AdminListAuditEvents RPC — entirely missing on identity-svc, so
     /admin/audit was a placeholder.
  2. §13.7 fields on AdminUpdateOrganization — the OrgDetail edit
     dialog only surfaced legal_name, type, tax_id, vat_id_eu, even
     though the backend handler ALREADY persisted headquarters_address
     and primary_admin_user_id.
  3. §13.8 fields on AdminUpdateUser — the UsersList edit dialog only
     surfaced first_name, last_name, email, phone_number, role,
     ui_language, even though the backend handler ALREADY persisted
     organization_id, default_modality_id, professional_title,
     credentials_number, biography, avatar_url, billing_address.

All three are now done.

(1) AdminListAuditEvents RPC
============================
Backend wiring is end-to-end on identity-svc.

Files:
- proto/identity/v1/identity.proto
  • added RPC AdminListAuditEvents on IdentityService.
  • added messages AdminListAuditEventsRequest (page_size, page_token,
    actor_email ILIKE, action exact, since/until Timestamp) and
    AdminListAuditEventsResponse (events, next_page_token).
- services/identity-svc/internal/adapters/postgres/queries/audit_events.sql
  • added AdminListAuditEvents :many. LEFT JOIN to users so each row
    carries actor_email without a second roundtrip. All filters AND
    together via "narg IS NULL OR …" patterns. Cursor pagination on
    (occurred_at, id) DESC matching the other admin lists.
- services/identity-svc/internal/adapters/grpc/admin.go
  • new handler AdminListAuditEvents. requireSuperwizorAdmin gate,
    pagesize clamp (default 50, cap 200), filter coercion, row →
    AuditEntry mapping, next_page_token emission. Returns 200 with
    empty list when filters exclude everything.
- services/identity-svc/internal/adapters/grpc/connect_adapter.go
  • Connect-RPC shim added so identityv1connect.IdentityServiceHandler
    is satisfied (build catches forgotten shims).
- Regenerated:
  • gen/go/identity/v1/identity.pb.go + identity_grpc.pb.go + identityv1connect/
  • gen/ts/identity/v1/identity_pb.ts
  • services/identity-svc/internal/adapters/postgres/db/audit_events.sql.go
  • services/identity-svc/internal/adapters/postgres/db/querier.go

Verification:
  go build ./...                          OK (all submodules)
  cd services/identity-svc && go test ./... → ok (2.124s)
    (The existing connect_adapter_test.go End-to-End test is the
    gatekeeper for the Connect interface — passing means the new
    AdminListAuditEvents shim wires through.)

(2) /admin/audit page — real list
==================================
The placeholder is gone. /admin/audit now renders AuditLogList which
calls AdminListAuditEvents.

Files:
- marketing-site/src/components/admin/AuditLogList.tsx (new)
  • Filters bar: actor_email (debounced search), action (curated
    KNOWN_ACTIONS dropdown + free), since (date), until (date).
  • Date inputs interpret "YYYY-MM-DD" as start/end of local day.
  • Table columns: occurred_at, actor, action, resource_type+id,
    reason. Same cursor-stack pagination pattern as OrgsList/
    UsersList.
- marketing-site/src/app/[locale]/admin/audit/page.tsx
  • Slimmed down to a server shell rendering <AuditLogList />.
  • Removed placeholderTitle/placeholderBody/goToOrgs translation
    keys (replaced with audit.* filter and column labels).
- marketing-site/messages/{pl,en}.json
  • admin.audit namespace rewritten: actorEmailLabel, actionLabel,
    anyAction, sinceLabel, untilLabel, loading, empty, error, retry,
    prev, next, col.{occurred,actor,action,resource,reason}.

(3) OrgEdit dialog — headquarters_address + primary_admin_user_id
==================================================================
The org-detail edit dialog now covers all §13.7 fields.

Files:
- marketing-site/src/components/admin/AddressFields.tsx (new)
  • Shared 8-input address sub-form (country_code, region, city,
    postal_code, street_line, building_number, unit_number,
    directions). Exports AddressDraft, EMPTY_ADDRESS, addressDiffers,
    addressFromProto helpers. Reused by both OrgEdit and UserEdit.
- marketing-site/src/components/admin/OrgDetail.tsx
  • Edit dialog draft state extended with primaryAdminUserId +
    address, plus a snapshot of the original values so submission
    only sends fields that actually changed.
  • Primary admin picker is a <select> sourced from
    details.therapists (already loaded). The hint text steers admins
    to first promote to ORG_ADMIN via user edit if the target isn't
    on the therapist roster.
  • AddressFields rendered below the existing fields, seeded from
    org.headquartersAddress.

- marketing-site/messages/{pl,en}.json
  • admin.orgEdit additions: addressTitle, primaryAdminLabel,
    primaryAdminUnchanged, primaryAdminHint.
  • new admin.address namespace: countryCode, region, city,
    postalCode, streetLine, buildingNumber, unitNumber, directions.

(4) UserEdit dialog — full §13.8 surface
========================================
The users-list edit dialog now covers all editable §13.8 fields.

Files:
- marketing-site/src/components/admin/UsersList.tsx
  • Imports AddressSchema + AddressFields helpers.
  • UserEditDialog draft state extended with: organizationId,
    defaultModalityId, professionalTitle, credentialsNumber,
    biography, avatarUrl, billingAddress.
  • Submission still uses the "only send what changed" pattern.
  • Two raw-UUID inputs (organizationId, defaultModalityId) with
    hint text explaining why no picker is available yet (no global
    org lookup; no ListModalities RPC). The backend rejects unknown
    UUIDs with InvalidArgument — admins won't silently lose data.
  • Billing address starts EMPTY (the User proto carries only
    billing_address_id, not the resolved Address). Any non-blank
    address field counts as a change.

- marketing-site/messages/{pl,en}.json
  • admin.users additions: professionalTitle, credentialsNumber,
    biography, avatarUrl, organizationId, organizationIdHint,
    defaultModalityId, defaultModalityIdHint, billingAddressTitle,
    billingAddressHint.

